  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM Ukraine Winterization Strategy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 24 February 2022, the Russian Federation launched a broad military offensive against Ukraine. The situation in the country quickly deteriorated, with major attacks reported across Ukraine, including in the capital, Kyiv. The overall scale and unpredictability of the situation requires immediate humanitarian assistance for the most vulnerable displaced and conflict-affected communities. The invasion has also exacerbated human suffering in eastern Ukraine, an area already affected by eight years of armed conflict, isolated communities, and a deteriorating infrastructure. With the onset of winter, Ukraine is approaching a compounded crisis, putting millions of already vulnerable people at greater risk given the country and district heating facilities and supply lines damaged in areas of physical conflict. This winterization proposal supports the Shelter, Non-Food Item (NFI), Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH), and Cash sectors with activities focused on specific winterization Shelter and NFI support, including winter items, items for heating and cash/voucher support specifically for winter items, and light repairs for collective centres through mobile teams; cash for rent; and WASH through specific repairs or inputs for infrastructure to withstand winter and support temperature control, and WASH NFIs.</narrative>
  </description>
